      "id": "sol.ahsme-1989-p14.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Using \\(\\sin10=2\\sin5\\cos5,\\) \\[ \\begin{aligned} \\cot10+\\tan5 &=\\frac{\\cos10}{\\sin10}\\\\ &\\quad+\\frac{\\sin5}{\\cos5}. \\end{aligned} \\] Combining the fractions gives numerator \\(\\cos10+2\\sin^25.\\) Since \\(\\cos10=\\cos^25-\\sin^25,\\) this numerator is \\(1,\\) and the expression is \\(\\csc10.\\)\n\nThus the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Rewrite both terms using sine and cosine",
        "Use \\(\\sin10=2\\sin5\\cos5\\) and \\(\\cos10=\\cos^25-\\sin^25\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
